-- title:
--   Common affine neighbourhoods in the smooth locus over an affine base
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and $M$ a nonzero natural number with $5 \le M$ and $p \nmid M$; let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero that is a cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ of order $p$, and let $\zeta \in L$ be a primitive $p$-th root of unity. Let $K$ be the intermediate field of $L \subseteq \mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ equal to [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L (ModularCurve.x1FunctionField (M * p))`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103), that is, the $L$-subfield generated by the image, under the coefficientwise map [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb L`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81) induced by $\mathbb{Q} \to L$, of the $q$-expansion function field of $\Gamma_1(Mp)$ inside $\mathbb{Q}((q))$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with an $L$-algebra structure making $L$ its fraction field, such that $p$ lies in the maximal ideal of $A$ and $\zeta$ lies in the image of $A \to L$, together with an $A$-algebra structure on $K$ compatible with that on $L$. Let $j \in K$ be nonzero with image in $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ the series [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb L ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81), where [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157) is $q^{-1}$ times the rational $j$-numerator power series. Write $X =$ [`ModularCurve.TwoChartModel A K j`](def/ModularCurve_TwoChartModel.html#L229) for the pushout of the two chart inclusions, with structure morphism $f =$ [`ModularCurve.TwoChart.modelTo A K j`](def/ModularCurve_TwoChartModel.html#L252) $: X \to \operatorname{Spec} A$. Let $U$ be an open subscheme of $X$ such that the inclusion $U \hookrightarrow X$ followed by $f$ is smooth of relative dimension $1$, and which is maximal with this property: every open $W \subseteq X$ whose inclusion followed by $f$ is smooth of relative dimension $1$ satisfies $W \le U$. The conclusion: for every affine open $V$ of $\operatorname{Spec} A$ and every finite set $F$ of points of $U$ all of whose images under $U \hookrightarrow X \to \operatorname{Spec} A$ lie in $V$, there is an open $W$ of the scheme $U$ which is affine, is contained in the preimage of $V$ under $U \hookrightarrow X \to \operatorname{Spec} A$, and contains every point of $F$.
--
--   This is the covering condition required by the representability criterion for the relative Picard functor: finitely many points of the smooth locus lying over a fixed affine of the base admit a single affine neighbourhood inside that locus. It is used by [`ModularCurve.XOneP.exists_representsRelSubPic_algEquivZeroCut_twoChartModel_x1_mul`](thm.html#ModularCurve.XOneP.exists_representsRelSubPic_algEquivZeroCut_twoChartModel_x1_mul), and is proved from the two-chart structure of the model together with the general statements [`AlgebraicGeometry.exists_isAffineOpen_forall_mem_of_finset_of_twoCharts`](thm.html#AlgebraicGeometry.exists_isAffineOpen_forall_mem_of_finset_of_twoCharts) and [`AlgebraicGeometry.exists_isAffineOpen_opens_le_preimage_forall_mem_of_forall_finset`](thm.html#AlgebraicGeometry.exists_isAffineOpen_opens_le_preimage_forall_mem_of_forall_finset).
